      "content": {
        "kind": "bundle",
        "sourceNeedCount": 5,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "summary",
            "heading": "Key ideas from this article",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Before the courses, the career question."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "These are ordered by growth headroom, not by prestige."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Do not buy a course until you know the track."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:1",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "B.tech ECE Degree Is Not the Problem",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Skill first, degree second, is a fair rule for most of the roles below."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A CSE student searching for courses is mostly choosing between skills inside one job family."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "track-first",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 1
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:3",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Led By How Far Each Can Scale",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "VLSI has a higher pay ceiling inside a company but a much narrower door."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "You write C on microcontrollers, talk to sensors over UART, SPI and I2C, and debug with a logic analyser when the code is right and the board still misbehaves."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "tracks",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 3
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:9",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Pay a Training Institute",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Some paid programmes do add value, especially where a college cannot supply tools or feedback."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A line like \"90% placed\" tells you nothing until you know how many joined, how many finished, and how many got a role that uses the skill you paid for."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Which boards, which EDA tools, how many hours per student on real tools."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "institute-test",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 9
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:11",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Four Questions for an ECE Course",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Before you commit money or a semester, put each course through the same four checks."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Where does your energy hold up: bench work and slow debugging, plant-side site visits and shifts, or a desk with code and simulators."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Be honest about how you like to work before paying for a board-based programme."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "checkpoint",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 11
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:12",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Top-Band Figures Are the Exception",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Blinking an LED with a library proves you can follow a tutorial."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A pile of IoT, PLC, VLSI, Python and cloud certificates without a project behind any one of them is a scattered profile."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "mistakes",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 12
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "ECE Career Options and Opportunities"
    },
